; HYPOTHETICAL -- not valid L0. What base64's main would be if standard
; output could report a failed write.
;
; One way: a builtin (flush h) that delivers any bytes held back for h,
; standard output included, and returns 0, or -5 if they could not be
; written, as close does for a file. The program flushes once, at the end,
; and turns a failure into an exit status, as every Unix filter does.

(def main () int
  (let st (if (eq (arg_count) 0)
              (encode 0 1 0)
              (decode 0 1 0 0))
    (if (lt (flush 1) 0)
        (let w (write_err "base64: write error\n") 1)
        st)))
